INT. COUNTY HOSPITAL - TRAUMA BAY 2 - NIGHT

White light, steel trays, the smell of antiseptic over blood. A monitor chirps. A man lies on the table under a sheet, chest open, a ventilator breathing for him.

DR. XIMENA FERREIRA, forties, scrubs soaked at the collar, hands buried in the incision, her gray eyes fixed on a point nobody else can see. Across the table, NURSE GLORIA, fifties, steady, passes instruments with the unhurried economy of someone who has done it ten thousand times.

An ORDERLY, twenties, tall, pressed against the wall near the door, holds a clipboard he has no reason to hold.

XIMENA
Suction.

Gloria obliges. The sound is wet and fast.

XIMENA (CONT'D)
Pressure?

GLORIA
Eighty over forty. Dropping.

XIMENA
(muttering)
Come on. Come on.

She reaches deeper. The monitor skips. The ORDERLY shifts, the clipboard rustles. Ximena doesn't look up.

XIMENA (CONT'D)
Whoever is breathing back there, stop.

ORDERLY
Sorry, Doctor.

XIMENA
Who are you?

ORDERLY
Transport. They said you needed hands.

XIMENA
I need hands that know what to do.

ORDERLY
I'm a med student. Third year. Tobias.

Gloria doesn't turn. Ximena exhales through her nose.

XIMENA
Tobias, scrub in. Now. Basin by the door.

TOBIAS
Yes, Doctor.

He moves. Scrubs, hands shaking. The water runs.

GLORIA
(to the room)
Everybody, quiet. She's going in for the clamp.

Silence. Ximena closes her fingers around something.

XIMENA
Got it.

The monitor chirps once, then twice, then a steadier rhythm.

GLORIA
Pressure's coming up. Ninety.

XIMENA
Hundred, Gloria. Say it with me.

GLORIA
Hundred.

Tobias, gloved now, edges to the table. Ximena nods at the retractor.

XIMENA
Hold that. Don't let go no matter what I say.

TOBIAS
What if I faint?

XIMENA
(without humor)
Then faint standing up.

The monitor holds a quiet, even tone. Tobias grips the retractor, white-knuckled, and does not let go.

XIMENA (CONT'D)
(muttering, almost a prayer)
Hold, hold, hold.
